# Copy to .env.prod on the server. NEVER commit the real file.
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=countdown
IMAGE_TAG=latest
SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=production
PGADMIN_PORT=5050
BACKUP_DIR=./backups
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=change-me
# comma-separated real GitHub logins granted the super-admin role; empty = nobody has it
SUPER_ADMIN_GITHUB_LOGINS=
PGADMIN_EMAIL=admin@local.dev
PGADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me
# Three Weltanschauung secrets: the browser Maps JavaScript API key (HTTP-referrer
# restricted), the server-only key for the backend's own Google calls (IP-restricted,
# never sent to a client), and the Street View Static API URL-signing secret. See
# core/README.md ("Weltanschauung: the two Maps keys and the signing secret") for exactly
# which Google Cloud API to enable and which restriction to set for each.
SPOT_OBJECT_MAPS_API_KEY=change-me
SPOT_OBJECT_SERVER_MAPS_API_KEY=change-me
SPOT_OBJECT_SIGNING_SECRET=change-me
# GUESS_HUE_DATASET_FILE is NOT set here: update.sh computes and exports it itself
# (see deploy/README.md) -- the shell environment outranks --env-file, so a value here would be dead text.
# SOPS_AGE_KEY_FILE does NOT belong here either: update.sh only passes this file on to compose
# via --env-file, it never sources it into its own shell. A value here would therefore never reach
# the sops call inside update.sh. A non-default key location (default ~/.config/sops/age/keys.txt)
# is set in the environment update.sh runs in instead, e.g.
# SOPS_AGE_KEY_FILE=/opt/unividuell/secrets/age.key ./update.sh prod
# (see deploy/README.md).
